<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olosega</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olosega is a small volcanic island in the Manuʻa group of American Samoa, linked to neighbouring Ofu by a bridge across a narrow channel. It has steep cliffs, and its small population lives in villages along the coast. Like the rest of Manuʻa, it was ceded to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> by the Tuʻi Manuʻa in 1904.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/olosega.jpg" alt="Olosega" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA, Original uploader: GarciaB · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ofu-OlosegaFromSpace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
